      "sourceTextSha256": "f896c59b873c0c221ee065a883570c2c544b72ffe3cd2d0daaf745a64a00b637",
      "text": "Day 4 · The Cotacachi-Cayapas Ecological Reserve, created in 1968 and covering some 243,600 hectares from about 35 m to 4,939 m at the summit of Cotacachi, with the condor as its emblem: a walk along the rim of Cuicocha Crater Lake and a boat ride. Then the El Ángel Reserve, with its endemic frailejones and one of the few Polylepis forests in the world; after dinner, a short torchlit walk among the ancient trees. Overnight at Polylepis Lodge. (B, D)",
